<title>GERMANY: Schmalbach buys Johnson unit.</title>
<headline>Schmalbach buys Johnson unit.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1997-03-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Germany's Schmalbach-Lubeca AG said on Tuesday it had bought the polyethylene terephthalate (PET) unit of U.S.-based Johnson Controls Inc for an undisclosed sum.</p>
<p>Last December, when Schmalbach confirmed it was interested in the business, its finance chief Jan Maarten Henderson told journalists a purchase price of around one billion marks would not be unreasonable.  </p>
<p>Schmalbach however declined to give any details on the cost of the deal, which will give it, a unit of Germany's VIAG AG, nearly 15 percent of the world's PET packaging business.</p>
<p>The move is part of an overall strategy to focus more on core activities, including PET packaging, beverage containers and container caps, the group said.</p>
<p>The new group will operate under the name of Schmalbach-Lubeca Plastic Containers USA Inc.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
</text>
